[Music]  thank you  I don't generally make build videos as  there are plenty of YouTubers out there  that cover the side of things already  but I keep getting asked what I'm  running in my last couple of videos so I  thought screw it I have some spare time  this afternoon and given the type of  build this is it should only take a few  minutes to run through I will never  claim a build as being the best of its  type because this is just something that  works for me with my style of play and  the platform I play on I'll always  recommend using these as a template for  yourself and adapt it based on your  needs there will always be another build  out there that will provide more DPS  survivability or whatever else you're  looking for  this Loadout is fully based around the  Striker's battle gear set since the  recent revamp of the set it has become  my most used build for General  activities mainly because I love doing  high damage however like most DPS builds  it comes with a drawback of lacking a  little on the survivability side of  things so as you'll soon see I've had to  pull back on a little bit of the damage  in order to counter this  I'm not going to read through the set  perks or each individual piece because  I'm sure you can read for yourself but  summing the setup shoot stuff do more  damage  I'm using four pieces of Strikers The  Mask backpack gloves and Holster  the backpack because it boosts the  damage from 0.65 to 1 per stack but I  don't bother with the chess piece I like  this piece in group play or in countdown  but when playing solo most waves of  enemy aren't large enough or have enough  hit points to really be able to take  advantage of the extra Stacks so instead  I run the chesca chest chesca chest yeah  with the obliterate Talent this provides  a damage boost that is more immediately  available during small encounters plus  it has the added brand set attribute of  plus 10 critical hit chance  on the knee pads I'm using yield  faithful Fox's prayer mainly for the  mock applicative plus eight percent  damage to targets out of cover  all pieces have been rolled into weapon  damage for the core attribute and  critical hit damage and all chance as  the secondary attribute  I'm not going to tell you where these  need to be placed as it will depend on  the pieces you have at your disposal  just try and get as close as you can to  60 critical hit chance and pump the  wrist into critical hit damage  on my build I have 56.5 critical hit  chance and 141 critical hit damage but  you should be able to squeeze a little  more out of this  the weapons are whatever you feel  comfortable with the Famas is one of my  favorites because of the ridiculous rate  of fire although this build provides a  little bit of weapon handling you may  still find The Recoil a little bit too  much to control so you could instead  look at the carbine 7 or the king  breaker with higher damage and lower RPM  the talent I've chucked onto this is  Preservation to help with survivability  the secondary weapon is the rock and  roll shotgun to build the stacks quickly  but to be completely honest with the  rate of fire of the Famas I don't use  this often you could instead use a  weapon with a little bit of range  especially if you were using an SMG as  humane  the specialization is gonna mainly  because of the 10 armor on kill and five  percent rate of fire on kill  the skills are reviver Hive and well  whatever you want there aren't any skill  tiers with this so you aren't going to  get a huge amount from whatever you run  anyway I'm using the fixodrone just to  help a little bit with countering the  incoming damage  and that's pretty much it you are still  very squishy but you pack a hell of a  punch make sure to utilize cover well  but you need to play aggressive and keep  killing in order to keep a steady stream  of armor coming in like I said earlier  there are a ton of ways to get much more  damage out of the set but as a solo  player on heroic this is more than  enough  thank you very much for watching and  I'll catch you in the next one  [Music]  [Music]

